<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{D^{2}}\sum_{i,j}\sum_{i^{\prime},j^{\prime}}w_{i}^{\mu}w_{j}^{\nu}w_{i^{\prime}}^{\mu}w_{j^{\prime}}^{\nu}\delta_{\mu\nu}\frac{\delta_{ii^{\prime}}}{D}\ab(w_{j}w_{j^{\prime}}+\frac{D}{L}\ab(1+\sigma^{2})\delta_{jj^{\prime}})+\mathcal{O}\ab(\frac{1}{D^{2}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>ν</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>ν</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\ab</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>D</mi><mi>L</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\ab</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\ab</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{D^{2}}\sum_{i,j}\sum_{i^{\prime},j^{\prime}}w_{i}^{\mu}w_{j}^{\nu}w_{i^{\prime}}^{\mu}w_{j^{\prime}}^{\nu}\delta_{\mu\nu}\frac{\delta_{ii^{\prime}}}{D}\ab(w_{j}w_{j^{\prime}}+\frac{D}{L}\ab(1+\sigma^{2})\delta_{jj^{\prime}})+\mathcal{O}\ab(\frac{1}{D^{2}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\delta_{\mu\nu}\ab(1+\sigma^{2})+\mathcal{O}\ab(\frac{1}{D})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\ab</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\ab</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\delta_{\mu\nu}\ab(1+\sigma^{2})+\mathcal{O}\ab(\frac{1}{D}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">which completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Relation to Committee Machine</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This process reveals a crucial distinction from conventional multi-teacher models like committee machines, which learn the average behavior of a teacher ensemble to capture their consensus.
Our student, in contrast, is not trained to find this middle ground but must learn to imitate every individual teacher.
Statement <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma C.2. ‣ C.1 Justification of Equivalence of the Linear Attention Model to a Many-Teacher-Student Model ‣ Appendix C Justification of Equivalence of the Linear Attention Model to a Many-Teacher-Student Model" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a> reveals that the essence of ICL is not knowledge aggregation, but the acquisition of a universal meta-algorithm capable of acting as any specialized teacher based on the context.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Preliminary Lemmas in Random Matrix Theory</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we provide the proofs for several technical lemmas required in the calculation of the replica method in the main text. These lemmas establish fundamental properties of random matrices that arise in our analysis, particularly concerning resolvent functions and their derivatives.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Resolvent Functions for Wishart-Type Matrices</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We begin by establishing the resolvent functions for a class of random matrices that play a central role in our replica calculation.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma D.1</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider the random matrix</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{S}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E45.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{D}{r}\frac{1}{M_{0}}\sum_{\mu=1}^{M_{0}}\mathbf{v}^{\mu}{\mathbf{v}^{\mu}}^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{r\times r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>D</mi><mi>r</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>𝐯</mi><mrow></mrow><mi>μ</mi><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{D}{r}\frac{1}{M_{0}}\sum_{\mu=1}^{M_{0}}\mathbf{v}^{\mu}{\mathbf{v}^{\mu}}^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{r\times r}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(45)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle S</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E46.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{D}{r}\frac{1}{M_{0}}\sum_{\mu=1}^{M_{0}}A\mathbf{v}^{\mu}{\mathbf{v}^{\mu}}^{\top}A^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times D}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>D</mi><mi>r</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>𝐯</mi><mrow></mrow><mi>μ</mi><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{D}{r}\frac{1}{M_{0}}\sum_{\mu=1}^{M_{0}}A\mathbf{v}^{\mu}{\mathbf{v}^{\mu}}^{\top}A^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times D},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(46)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;r&lt;D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;r&lt;D</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}^{\mu}\in\mathbb{R}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}^{\mu}\in\mathbb{R}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math> are random standard normal vectors and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times r}</annotation></semantics></math> is a random orthogonal basis.
Then, the resolvent of <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{S}</annotation></semantics></math> are given by</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle g_{\tilde{S}}(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle g_{\tilde{S}}(z)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E47.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{D}\tr\ab(\ab(\tilde{S}-zI_{D})^{-1})=\frac{-(\kappa\rho z+\rho-\kappa)-\sqrt{\left(\kappa\rho z+\rho-\kappa\right)^{2}-4\rho^{2}\kappa z}}{2\rho z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mtext class="undefined">\ab</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="undefined">\ab</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{D}\tr\ab(\ab(\tilde{S}-zI_{D})^{-1})=\frac{-(\kappa\rho z+\rho-\kappa)-\sqrt{\left(\kappa\rho z+\rho-\kappa\right)^{2}-4\rho^{2}\kappa z}}{2\rho z}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(47)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle g_{S}(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle g_{S}(z)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E48.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{D}\tr\ab(\ab({S}-zI_{D})^{-1})=\frac{\kappa+\rho-\kappa\rho z-2-\sqrt{\left(\rho\kappa z+\rho-\kappa\right)^{2}-4\rho^{2}\kappa z}}{2z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mtext class="undefined">\ab</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="undefined">\ab</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{D}\tr\ab(\ab({S}-zI_{D})^{-1})=\frac{\kappa+\rho-\kappa\rho z-2-\sqrt{\left(\rho\kappa z+\rho-\kappa\right)^{2}-4\rho^{2}\kappa z}}{2z}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(48)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> respectively, where <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=r/D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=r/D</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa=M_{0}/D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa=M_{0}/D</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D,r,M_{0}\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D,r,M_{0}\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">The random matrix <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{S}</annotation></semantics></math> is classified as a Wishart matrix (or a scaled sample covariance matrix).
The empirical spectral distribution of such a matrix is known to converge to the Marchenko-Pastur distribution in the given asymptotic limit.
Therefore, Eq. (<a href="#A4.E47" title="In Lemma D.1. ‣ D.1 Resolvent Functions for Wishart-Type Matrices ‣ Appendix D Preliminary Lemmas in Random Matrix Theory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">47</span></a>), which represents its Stieltjes transform, follows directly from this standard result in random matrix theory (e.g., see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Potters and Bouchaud, 2020</a>]</cite>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">For the random matrix <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{S}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{S}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\tilde{S}}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\tilde{S}}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the characteristic polynomials of <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{S}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.
Then we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P_{S}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P_{S}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E49.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\det\ab(\lambda I_{D}-S)=\lambda^{D-r}\det\ab(\lambda I_{r}-\tilde{S})=\lambda^{D-r}P_{\tilde{S}}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>det</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mtext class="undefined">\ab</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>det</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mtext class="undefined">\ab</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\det\ab(\lambda I_{D}-S)=\lambda^{D-r}\det\ab(\lambda I_{r}-\tilde{S})=\lambda^{D-r}P_{\tilde{S}}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(49)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">which implies that the non-zero eigen values of <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{S}</annotation></semantics></math> coincide, including multiplicities.
Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle g_{S}(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle g_{S}(z)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E50.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\frac{D-r}{D}\frac{1}{z}+\frac{r}{D}g_{\tilde{S}}(z)=-\ab(1-\rho)\frac{1}{z}+\rho g_{\tilde{S}}(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>z</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>r</mi><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mtext class="undefined">\ab</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>z</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\frac{D-r}{D}\frac{1}{z}+\frac{r}{D}g_{\tilde{S}}(z)=-\ab(1-\rho)\frac{1}{z}+\rho g_{\tilde{S}}(z)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(50)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{D}\tr\ab(\ab({S}-zI_{D})^{-1})=\frac{\kappa+\rho-\kappa\rho z-2-\sqrt{\left(\rho\kappa z+\rho-\kappa\right)^{2}-4\rho^{2}\kappa z}}{2z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mtext class="undefined">\ab</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="undefined">\ab</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{D}\tr\ab(\ab({S}-zI_{D})^{-1})=\frac{\kappa+\rho-\kappa\rho z-2-\sqrt{\left(\rho\kappa z+\rho-\kappa\right)^{2}-4\rho^{2}\kappa z}}{2z}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(51)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">as desired in Eq. (<a href="#A4.E48" title="In Lemma D.1. ‣ D.1 Resolvent Functions for Wishart-Type Matrices ‣ Appendix D Preliminary Lemmas in Random Matrix Theory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">48</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Recurrence Relations for Matrix Moments</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Having established the resolvent functions, we now derive recurrence relations that allow us to compute higher-order moments involving powers of the random matrices and their resolvents.
These relations are essential for the subsequent calculations in the saddle-point equations.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma D.2</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}=aS+bI_{D}\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}=aS+bI_{D}\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times D}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,b&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a,b&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> is defined in Lemma <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma D.1. ‣ D.1 Resolvent Functions for Wishart-Type Matrices ‣ Appendix D Preliminary Lemmas in Random Matrix Theory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a>. Define <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{n,m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{n,m}</annotation></semantics></math> by</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle E_{n,m}=\frac{1}{D}\mathbb{E}\ab[\tr S^{n}\mathcal{M}^{-m}]=\frac{1}{D}\mathbb{E}\ab[\tr S^{n}(aS+bI_{D})^{-m}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\ab</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\ab</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle E_{n,m}=\frac{1}{D}\mathbb{E}\ab[\tr S^{n}\mathcal{M}^{-m}]=\frac{1}{D}\mathbb{E}\ab[\tr S^{n}(aS+bI_{D})^{-m}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(52)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for integer <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n,m\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n,m\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, the following recurrence relation holds:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle E_{0,m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle E_{0,m}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E53.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{b^{m}}\frac{1}{(m-1)!}g_{S}^{(m-1)}(z)\quad(\text{for }m\geq 1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>b</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>S</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for </mtext><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{b^{m}}\frac{1}{(m-1)!}g_{S}^{(m-1)}(z)\quad(\text{for }m\geq 1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(53)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle E_{n,0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle E_{n,0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E54.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=1\quad(n\geq 1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=1\quad(n\geq 1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(54)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle E_{n,m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle E_{n,m}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E55.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{b}E_{n-1,m-1}+zE_{n-1,m}\quad(n\geq 1,m\geq 1)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>b</mi></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{b}E_{n-1,m-1}+zE_{n-1,m}\quad(n\geq 1,m\geq 1),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(55)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="z=-b/a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=-b/a</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{(m-1)}_{S}(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>S</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{(m-1)}_{S}(z)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m-1)</annotation></semantics></math>-th derivative of <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{S}(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{S}(z)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">The inverse powers of <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> are given by:</span></p>
<table id="A4.E56" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}^{-m}=\frac{1}{b^{m}}(S-zI_{D})^{-m}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>b</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}^{-m}=\frac{1}{b^{m}}(S-zI_{D})^{-m}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(56)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">We use the standard definition of the Stieltjes transform, <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{S}(z)=\frac{1}{D}\mathbb{E}[\text{tr}((S-zI_{D})^{-1})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mtext>tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{S}(z)=\frac{1}{D}\mathbb{E}[\text{tr}((S-zI_{D})^{-1})]</annotation></semantics></math>.
The <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th derivative of the resolvent <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(S-zI_{D})^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(S-zI_{D})^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math> is:</span></p>
<table id="A4.E57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d^{k}}{dz^{k}}(S-zI_{D})^{-1}=k!(S-zI_{D})^{-(k+1)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d^{k}}{dz^{k}}(S-zI_{D})^{-1}=k!(S-zI_{D})^{-(k+1)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(57)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">From this, we can express the <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>-th power of the resolvent as:</span></p>
<table id="A4.E58" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(S-zI_{D})^{-m}=\frac{1}{(m-1)!}\frac{d^{m-1}}{dz^{m-1}}(S-zI_{D})^{-1}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(S-zI_{D})^{-m}=\frac{1}{(m-1)!}\frac{d^{m-1}}{dz^{m-1}}(S-zI_{D})^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(58)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">The <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th derivative of the Stieltjes transform is therefore:</span></p>
<table id="A4.E59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{S}^{(k)}(z)=\frac{d^{k}g_{S}(z)}{dz^{k}}=\frac{1}{D}\mathbb{E}\left[\tr\left(\frac{d^{k}}{dz^{k}}(S-zI_{D})^{-1}\right)\right]=\frac{k!}{D}\mathbb{E}\left[\text{tr}\left((S-zI_{D})^{-(k+1)}\right)\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>S</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow><mi>D</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mtext>tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{S}^{(k)}(z)=\frac{d^{k}g_{S}(z)}{dz^{k}}=\frac{1}{D}\mathbb{E}\left[\tr\left(\frac{d^{k}}{dz^{k}}(S-zI_{D})^{-1}\right)\right]=\frac{k!}{D}\mathbb{E}\left[\text{tr}\left((S-zI_{D})^{-(k+1)}\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(59)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">First, we prove the expression for <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{0,m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{0,m}</annotation></semantics></math>. By definition, for <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E60"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle E_{0,m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle E_{0,m}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E60.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{D}\mathbb{E}\left[\text{tr}(\mathcal{M}^{-m})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mtext>tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{D}\mathbb{E}\left[\text{tr}(\mathcal{M}^{-m})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(60)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E61"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{D}\mathbb{E}\left[\text{tr}\left(\frac{1}{b^{m}}(S-zI_{D})^{-m}\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mtext>tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>b</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{D}\mathbb{E}\left[\text{tr}\left(\frac{1}{b^{m}}(S-zI_{D})^{-m}\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(61)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E62"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{b^{m}}\frac{1}{D}\mathbb{E}\left[\tr\left(\frac{1}{(m-1)!}\frac{d^{m-1}}{dz^{m-1}}(S-zI_{D})^{-1}\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>b</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{b^{m}}\frac{1}{D}\mathbb{E}\left[\tr\left(\frac{1}{(m-1)!}\frac{d^{m-1}}{dz^{m-1}}(S-zI_{D})^{-1}\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(62)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{b^{m}}\frac{g_{S}^{(m-1)}(z)}{(m-1)!}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>b</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>S</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{b^{m}}\frac{g_{S}^{(m-1)}(z)}{(m-1)!}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(63)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Second, the expression for <math id="A4.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{n,0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{n,0}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A4.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> follows directly from the definition:</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{n,0}=\frac{1}{D}\mathbb{E}\left[\tr(S^n \mathcal{M}^0)\right]=\frac{1}{D}\mathbb{E}\left[\text{tr}(S^{n})\right]=1" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mtext>tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{n,0}=\frac{1}{D}\mathbb{E}\left[\tr(S^n \mathcal{M}^0)\right]=\frac{1}{D}\mathbb{E}\left[\text{tr}(S^{n})\right]=1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Third, we prove the recurrence relation for <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. We start from the definition of <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{n,m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{n,m}</annotation></semantics></math> and use the identity <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{n}=S^{n-1}((S-zI_{D})+zI_{D})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{n}=S^{n-1}((S-zI_{D})+zI_{D})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E64"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle E_{n,m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle E_{n,m}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E64.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{D}\mathbb{E}\left[\tr(S^n \mathcal{M}^{-m})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{D}\mathbb{E}\left[\tr(S^n \mathcal{M}^{-m})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(64)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E65"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{D}\mathbb{E}\left[\tr\left(\left(S^{n-1}(S-zI_{D})+zS^{n-1}\right)\mathcal{M}^{-m}\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{D}\mathbb{E}\left[\tr\left(\left(S^{n-1}(S-zI_{D})+zS^{n-1}\right)\mathcal{M}^{-m}\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(65)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E66"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{D}\mathbb{E}\left[\tr\left(S^{n-1}(S-zI_{D})\mathcal{M}^{-m}\right)\right]+\frac{1}{D}\mathbb{E}\left[\text{tr}\left(zS^{n-1}\mathcal{M}^{-m}\right)\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mtext>tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{D}\mathbb{E}\left[\tr\left(S^{n-1}(S-zI_{D})\mathcal{M}^{-m}\right)\right]+\frac{1}{D}\mathbb{E}\left[\text{tr}\left(zS^{n-1}\mathcal{M}^{-m}\right)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(66)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">For the first term of Eq. (<a href="#A4.E66" title="In Proof. ‣ D.2 Recurrence Relations for Matrix Moments ‣ Appendix D Preliminary Lemmas in Random Matrix Theory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">66</span></a>), we substitute <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(S-zI_{D})=\frac{1}{b}\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>b</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(S-zI_{D})=\frac{1}{b}\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A4.E67" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{D}\mathbb{E}\left[\text{tr}\left(S^{n-1}(S-zI_{D})\mathcal{M}^{-m}\right)\right]=\frac{1}{b}\frac{1}{D}\mathbb{E}\left[\text{tr}\left(S^{n-1}\mathcal{M}^{-(m-1)}\right)\right]=\frac{1}{b}E_{n-1,m-1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mtext>tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>b</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mtext>tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>b</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{D}\mathbb{E}\left[\text{tr}\left(S^{n-1}(S-zI_{D})\mathcal{M}^{-m}\right)\right]=\frac{1}{b}\frac{1}{D}\mathbb{E}\left[\text{tr}\left(S^{n-1}\mathcal{M}^{-(m-1)}\right)\right]=\frac{1}{b}E_{n-1,m-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(67)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">The second term is:</span></p>
<table id="A4.E68" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{D}\mathbb{E}\left[\text{tr}\left(zS^{n-1}\mathcal{M}^{-m}\right)\right]=z\left(\frac{1}{D}\mathbb{E}\left[\text{tr}\left(S^{n-1}\mathcal{M}^{-m}\right)\right]\right)=zE_{n-1,m}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mtext>tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mtext>tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{D}\mathbb{E}\left[\text{tr}\left(zS^{n-1}\mathcal{M}^{-m}\right)\right]=z\left(\frac{1}{D}\mathbb{E}\left[\text{tr}\left(S^{n-1}\mathcal{M}^{-m}\right)\right]\right)=zE_{n-1,m}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(68)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">Combining the two terms gives the recurrence relation:</span></p>
<table id="A4.E69" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{n,m}=\frac{1}{b}E_{n-1,m-1}+zE_{n-1,m}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>b</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{n,m}=\frac{1}{b}E_{n-1,m-1}+zE_{n-1,m},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(69)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p5.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p5.5.1" class="ltx_text">which completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3 </span>Explicit Expressions for Matrix Moments</h3>

<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The recurrence relations established in the previous lemma can be used to derive explicit expressions for specific combinations of matrix powers and resolvents that frequently appear in our calculations.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition D.3</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math> be as defined in Lemma <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma D.1. ‣ D.1 Resolvent Functions for Wishart-Type Matrices ‣ Appendix D Preliminary Lemmas in Random Matrix Theory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a> and <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma D.2. ‣ D.2 Recurrence Relations for Matrix Moments ‣ Appendix D Preliminary Lemmas in Random Matrix Theory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a>. Then, the following relations hold:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E70"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{D}\mathbb{E}\ab[\tr\mathcal{M}^{-1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\ab</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{D}\mathbb{E}\ab[\tr\mathcal{M}^{-1}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E70.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{g_{S}(z)}{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>b</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{g_{S}(z)}{b}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(70)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E71"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{D}\mathbb{E}\ab[\tr\mathcal{M}^{-2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\ab</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{D}\mathbb{E}\ab[\tr\mathcal{M}^{-2}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E71.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{g_{S}^{\prime}(z)}{b^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{g_{S}^{\prime}(z)}{b^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(71)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E72"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{D}\mathbb{E}\ab[\tr S\mathcal{M}^{-1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\ab</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{D}\mathbb{E}\ab[\tr S\mathcal{M}^{-1}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E72.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1+zg_{S}(z)}{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>b</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1+zg_{S}(z)}{b}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(72)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E73"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{D}\mathbb{E}\ab[\tr S\mathcal{M}^{-2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\ab</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{D}\mathbb{E}\ab[\tr S\mathcal{M}^{-2}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E73.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{g_{S}(z)+zg_{S}^{\prime}(z)}{b^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{g_{S}(z)+zg_{S}^{\prime}(z)}{b^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(73)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E74"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{D}\mathbb{E}\ab[\tr S^{2}\mathcal{M}^{-1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\ab</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{D}\mathbb{E}\ab[\tr S^{2}\mathcal{M}^{-1}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E74.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1+z+z^{2}g_{S}(z)}{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>b</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1+z+z^{2}g_{S}(z)}{b}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(74)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E75"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{D}\mathbb{E}\ab[\tr S^{2}\mathcal{M}^{-2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\ab</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{D}\mathbb{E}\ab[\tr S^{2}\mathcal{M}^{-2}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E75.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1+2zg_{S}(z)+z^{2}g_{S}^{\prime}(z)}{b^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1+2zg_{S}(z)+z^{2}g_{S}^{\prime}(z)}{b^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(75)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E76"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{D}\mathbb{E}\ab[\tr S^{3}\mathcal{M}^{-2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\ab</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{D}\mathbb{E}\ab[\tr S^{3}\mathcal{M}^{-2}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E76.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1+2z+3z^{2}g_{S}(z)+z^{3}g_{S}^{\prime}(z)}{b^{2}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1+2z+3z^{2}g_{S}(z)+z^{3}g_{S}^{\prime}(z)}{b^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(76)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">The proof follows directly from Lemma <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma D.2. ‣ D.2 Recurrence Relations for Matrix Moments ‣ Appendix D Preliminary Lemmas in Random Matrix Theory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.4 </span>Trace Identity for Projected Matrices</h3>

<div id="A4.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, we establish a trace identity that relates the trace of a projected matrix to the trace of its lower-dimensional counterpart.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma D.4</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{S}</annotation></semantics></math> be as defined in Lemma <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma D.1. ‣ D.1 Resolvent Functions for Wishart-Type Matrices ‣ Appendix D Preliminary Lemmas in Random Matrix Theory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a>.
For scalars <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,b,l&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a,b,l&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, the following identity holds:</span></p>
<table id="A4.E77" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tr\left(AA^{\top}(aS+bI_{D})^{-l}\right)=\tr\left((a\tilde{S}+bI_{r})^{-l}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tr\left(AA^{\top}(aS+bI_{D})^{-l}\right)=\tr\left((a\tilde{S}+bI_{r})^{-l}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(77)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We prove this identity by performing a change of basis.
Since the <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> columns of <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> are orthonormal, we can extend this set to form a complete orthonormal basis for <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times(D-r)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times(D-r)}</annotation></semantics></math> be a matrix whose columns form an orthonormal basis for the orthogonal complement of the column space of <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>.
The resulting matrix <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U=[A\,B]\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U=[A\,B]\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times D}</annotation></semantics></math> is an orthogonal matrix, satisfying <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{\top}U=UU^{\top}=I_{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{\top}U=UU^{\top}=I_{D}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">The condition <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AA^{\top}S=S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AA^{\top}S=S</annotation></semantics></math> implies that the column space of <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> is contained within that of <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>.
Consequently, <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> must annihilate any vector orthogonal to the column space of <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>.
This means <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B^{\top}S=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{\top}S=0</annotation></semantics></math>, which can be verified as follows:</span></p>
<table id="A4.E78" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B^{\top}S=B^{\top}(AA^{\top}S)=(B^{\top}A)A^{\top}S=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{\top}S=B^{\top}(AA^{\top}S)=(B^{\top}A)A^{\top}S=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(78)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">In the new basis defined by <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>, the matrix <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> is represented by <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{\top}SU" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{\top}SU</annotation></semantics></math>. This similarity transformation reveals a block upper-triangular structure:</span></p>
<table id="A4.E79" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{\top}SU=\begin{pmatrix}A^{\top}B^{\top}\end{pmatrix}S\begin{pmatrix}A&amp;B\end{pmatrix}=\begin{pmatrix}A^{\top}SA&amp;A^{\top}SB\\
B^{\top}SA&amp;B^{\top}SB\end{pmatrix}=\begin{pmatrix}A^{\top}SA&amp;A^{\top}SB\\
0&amp;0\end{pmatrix}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable displaystyle="true"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true"><mtr><mtd><mi>A</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>B</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{\top}SU=\begin{pmatrix}A^{\top}B^{\top}\end{pmatrix}S\begin{pmatrix}A&amp;B\end{pmatrix}=\begin{pmatrix}A^{\top}SA&amp;A^{\top}SB\\
B^{\top}SA&amp;B^{\top}SB\end{pmatrix}=\begin{pmatrix}A^{\top}SA&amp;A^{\top}SB\\
0&amp;0\end{pmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(79)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Now, we express the left-hand side (LHS) of Eq. (<a href="#A4.E79" title="In Proof. ‣ D.4 Trace Identity for Projected Matrices ‣ Appendix D Preliminary Lemmas in Random Matrix Theory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">79</span></a>) in this basis. Using the cyclic property of the trace, <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tr(X)=\tr(U^\top X U)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tr(X)=\tr(U^\top X U)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A4.E80" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{LHS}=\tr\left(U^{\top}(AA^{\top})UU^{\top}(aS+bI_{D})^{-l}U\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>LHS</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{LHS}=\tr\left(U^{\top}(AA^{\top})UU^{\top}(aS+bI_{D})^{-l}U\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(80)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">The projection matrix <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AA^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AA^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> and the term <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(aS+bI_{D})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(aS+bI_{D})</annotation></semantics></math> transform as:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E81"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E81.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle U^{\top}AA^{\top}U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle U^{\top}AA^{\top}U</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E81.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\begin{pmatrix}I_{r}&amp;0\\
0&amp;0\end{pmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\begin{pmatrix}I_{r}&amp;0\\
0&amp;0\end{pmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(81)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E82"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle U^{\top}(aS+bI_{D})U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle U^{\top}(aS+bI_{D})U</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E82.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=a(U^{\top}SU)+bI_{D}=\begin{pmatrix}aA^{\top}SA+bI_{r}&amp;aA^{\top}SB\\
0&amp;bI_{D-r}\end{pmatrix}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=a(U^{\top}SU)+bI_{D}=\begin{pmatrix}aA^{\top}SA+bI_{r}&amp;aA^{\top}SB\\
0&amp;bI_{D-r}\end{pmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(82)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p3.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text">The inverse of a block upper-triangular matrix is also block upper-triangular, and squaring it preserves this structure. We only need the diagonal blocks for the trace calculation:</span></p>
<table id="A4.E83" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E83.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(U^{\top}(aS+bI_{D})U\right)^{-l}=\begin{pmatrix}(aA^{\top}SA+bI_{r})^{-l}&amp;*\\
0&amp;(bI_{D-r})^{-l}\end{pmatrix}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msup></mtd><mtd><mo>∗</mo></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msup></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(U^{\top}(aS+bI_{D})U\right)^{-l}=\begin{pmatrix}(aA^{\top}SA+bI_{r})^{-l}&amp;*\\
0&amp;(bI_{D-r})^{-l}\end{pmatrix},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(83)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p3.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p3.6.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="*" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∗</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">*</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the off-diagonal block, which is irrelevant for the trace. Substituting these into the expression for the LHS:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E84"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E84.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{LHS}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>LHS</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{LHS}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E84.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\tr\left(\begin{pmatrix}I_{r}&amp;0\\
0&amp;0\end{pmatrix}\begin{pmatrix}(aA^{\top}SA+bI_{r})^{-l}&amp;*\\
0&amp;b^{-l}I_{D-r}\end{pmatrix}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msup></mtd><mtd><mo>∗</mo></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\tr\left(\begin{pmatrix}I_{r}&amp;0\\
0&amp;0\end{pmatrix}\begin{pmatrix}(aA^{\top}SA+bI_{r})^{-l}&amp;*\\
0&amp;b^{-l}I_{D-r}\end{pmatrix}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(84)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E85"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E85.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\tr\begin{pmatrix}(aA^{\top}SA+bI_{r})^{-l}&amp;*\\
0&amp;0\end{pmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msup></mtd><mtd><mo>∗</mo></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\tr\begin{pmatrix}(aA^{\top}SA+bI_{r})^{-l}&amp;*\\
0&amp;0\end{pmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(85)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E86"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E86.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\tr\ab((aA^{\top}SA+bI_{r})^{-l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mtext class="undefined">\ab</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\tr\ab((aA^{\top}SA+bI_{r})^{-l})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(86)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p3.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p3.7.1" class="ltx_text">This is identical to the right-hand side of the proposition, which completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Replica Calculation</h2>

<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1 </span>Results with Complete Statements</h3>

<div id="A5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this subsection, we present the main results (Result  <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Result 3.1 (Decomposition of ICL prediction). ‣ 3 Decomposition of ICL Prediction" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>, <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Result 3.2 (Asymptotic Characterization of the Components). ‣ 3 Decomposition of ICL Prediction" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>, <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Result 4.1 (Effective Objective Function). ‣ 4.2 Theoretical Explanation ‣ 4 Finite Pre-training Data Induces Implicit Regularization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>, <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem2" title="Result 4.2 (Asymptotics of Regularization). ‣ 4.2 Theoretical Explanation ‣ 4 Finite Pre-training Data Induces Implicit Regularization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>, <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem2" title="Result 5.2. ‣ 5.2 Phase Transition in ICL Capabilities ‣ 5 Trade-offs from Task Difficulty" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a>) with complete statements, including the expression for the generalization error, which are derived using the replica method.
We analyze a more general model that incorporates a regularization term into the loss function. The results for the unregularized model can be recovered by simply setting the regularization strength <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_result">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Result E.1</span></span><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(Complete Statement of Optimal Parameter Matrix)
Let the optimal parameter matrix <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{*}\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{*}\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times D}</annotation></semantics></math> be the solution that minimizes the cost function <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}(W)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(W)</annotation></semantics></math>, defined as:</span></p>
<table id="A5.E87" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E87.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}(W)=\frac{1}{2}\sum_{\mu=1}^{M}\ab(\sum_{i=1}^{D}\sum_{j=1}^{D}\ab(\frac{w_{i}^{\mu}w_{j}^{\mu}}{D}-W_{ij})H_{ij}^{\mu})^{2}+\frac{M_{0}\lambda}{2}\sum_{i=1}^{D}\sum_{j=1}^{D}W_{ij}^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><mrow><mtext class="undefined">\ab</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>D</mi></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>D</mi></munderover><mrow><mtext class="undefined">\ab</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mi>D</mi></mfrac><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>D</mi></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>D</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(W)=\frac{1}{2}\sum_{\mu=1}^{M}\ab(\sum_{i=1}^{D}\sum_{j=1}^{D}\ab(\frac{w_{i}^{\mu}w_{j}^{\mu}}{D}-W_{ij})H_{ij}^{\mu})^{2}+\frac{M_{0}\lambda}{2}\sum_{i=1}^{D}\sum_{j=1}^{D}W_{ij}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(87)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For a given fixed set of tasks <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{0}=\{\mathbf{w}^{1},\dots,\mathbf{w}^{M_{0}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{0}=\{\mathbf{w}^{1},\dots,\mathbf{w}^{M_{0}}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exist non-negative scalar constants <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{q},\hat{m},\hat{\chi},\hat{\bar{q}},\hat{\bar{\chi}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>m</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>χ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>χ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{q},\hat{m},\hat{\chi},\hat{\bar{q}},\hat{\bar{\chi}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that the optimal matrix <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is given by the expression:</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E88"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E88.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W^{*}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E88.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{\mathrm{d}}{=}\argmin_{W}\ab[\frac{\lambda+\hat{\bar{q}}}{2}\tr\ab(WW^{\top})+\frac{\hat{q}}{2}\tr\ab(WSW^{\top})-\tr\ab(\ab(\sqrt{\hat{\chi}}T+\sqrt{\hat{\bar{\chi}}}R+\hat{m}S)W^{\top})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">d</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">argmin</mo><mi>W</mi></msub><mtext class="undefined">\ab</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>+</mo><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mtext class="undefined">\ab</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mtext class="undefined">\ab</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mtext class="undefined">\ab</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="undefined">\ab</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mover accent="true"><mi>χ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>χ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>^</mo></mover></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>m</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{\mathrm{d}}{=}\argmin_{W}\ab[\frac{\lambda+\hat{\bar{q}}}{2}\tr\ab(WW^{\top})+\frac{\hat{q}}{2}\tr\ab(WSW^{\top})-\tr\ab(\ab(\sqrt{\hat{\chi}}T+\sqrt{\hat{\bar{\chi}}}R+\hat{m}S)W^{\top})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(88)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.E89"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E89.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{\mathrm{d}}{=}\ab(\sqrt{\hat{\chi}}T+\sqrt{\hat{\bar{\chi}}}R+\hat{m}S)\ab(\hat{q}S+\ab(\lambda+\hat{\bar{q}})I_{D})^{-1}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">d</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\ab</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mover accent="true"><mi>χ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>χ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>^</mo></mover></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>m</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\ab</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mtext class="undefined">\ab</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>+</mo><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{\mathrm{d}}{=}\ab(\sqrt{\hat{\chi}}T+\sqrt{\hat{\bar{\chi}}}R+\hat{m}S)\ab(\hat{q}S+\ab(\lambda+\hat{\bar{q}})I_{D})^{-1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(89)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where the matrices <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T,R,S\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T,R,S\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times D}</annotation></semantics></math> are defined as follows:</span></p>
<table id="A5.E90" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E90.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=\frac{1}{M_{0}}\sum_{\mu=1}^{M_{0}}\mathbf{\xi}{\mathbf{w}^{\mu}}^{\top},\quad R=\ab(R_{ij})_{i,j=1}^{D}\sim\mathcal{N}\ab(0,\frac{1}{M_{0}}),\quad S=\frac{1}{M_{0}}\sum_{\mu=1}^{M_{0}}\mathbf{w}^{\mu}{\mathbf{w}^{\mu}}^{\top}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></munderover><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>𝐰</mi><mrow></mrow><mi>μ</mi><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext class="undefined">\ab</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>D</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\ab</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></munderover><mrow><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>𝐰</mi><mrow></mrow><mi>μ</mi><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=\frac{1}{M_{0}}\sum_{\mu=1}^{M_{0}}\mathbf{\xi}{\mathbf{w}^{\mu}}^{\top},\quad R=\ab(R_{ij})_{i,j=1}^{D}\sim\mathcal{N}\ab(0,\frac{1}{M_{0}}),\quad S=\frac{1}{M_{0}}\sum_{\mu=1}^{M_{0}}\mathbf{w}^{\mu}{\mathbf{w}^{\mu}}^{\top},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(90)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">with <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\xi}\in\mathbb{R}^{D}\sim\mathcal{N}\ab(0,I_{D})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\ab</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\xi}\in\mathbb{R}^{D}\sim\mathcal{N}\ab(0,I_{D})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_result">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Result E.2</span></span><span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(Parameter Derivation)

The order parameters <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q,m,q_{0},m_{0},\bar{q},\bar{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>m</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q,m,q_{0},m_{0},\bar{q},\bar{m}</annotation></semantics></math> (with auxiliary parameters <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>χ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi</annotation></semantics></math>) in Result. <a href="#A5.Thmtheorem1" title="Result E.1. ‣ E.1 Results with Complete Statements ‣ Appendix E Replica Calculation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.1</span></a>
and the conjugate parameters <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{q},\hat{m},\hat{\chi},\hat{\bar{q}},\hat{\bar{\chi}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>m</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>χ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>χ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{q},\hat{m},\hat{\chi},\hat{\bar{q}},\hat{\bar{\chi}}</annotation></semantics></math> in Result. <a href="#A5.Thmtheorem3" title="Result E.3. ‣ E.1 Results with Complete Statements ‣ Appendix E Replica Calculation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.3</span></a> are given by the solution of the following system of equations:</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E91"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E91.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q</annotation></semantics></math></td>
